WEBVTT

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:21.040
RAS! RAS! RAS! RAS!

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.380
Big Sis?

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.290
Congratulations, everyone!

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:43.290
What a marvelous show!

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.750
Today, we hold a party
in celebration of your success.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.460
Go nuts and enjoy yourselves!

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.540
The food looks good...

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:50.750
CHU2-sama!

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.040
I was in such a daze back there...

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.130
The whole thing's kind of a blur...

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.880
Then allow me to burn the image
of perfection into your brain!

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.000
How embarrassin'...!

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.500
Take a good, long look.
Talk about a breathtaking performance!

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:10.960
R-right...

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.380
Roselia's performance was
wonderful too, don't you think?

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.540
Yes. However, the winner...

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.630
...was RAISE A SUILEN!

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:18.420
Exactly!

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:21.580
And with our victory,
RAS has finally received justice!

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:22.790
MASKING...

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:24.040
Break out the strawberry cake!

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.790
Can't. I burned it...

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.540
Th-the next one better be huge!

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:32.880
Two layers with tons of strawberries!

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.210
Go ahead. Bon appetite!

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.040
Sure...

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.630
There's cabbage, too!

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:41.290
You brought all our favorite foods, didn't you?

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.880
Initial, I can't hide this passion in my heart

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.670
A sudden urge, and emotion flies from my fingertips!

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:13.290
On that fateful day, I was neither a child nor an adult

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:18.250
Gazing unwaveringly at my dream and nothing else

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:23.290
Feelings overflowing in the night, flaring and flickering

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:28.380
I gathered my courage and set out on a journey

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:33.710
Initial, it came bubbling to the surface

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:38.500
My entire body shivering with emotion

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:43.380
Why do I keep staring up at the endless night sky

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:49.250
And crying out the same words over and over?

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:53.130
Although I tend to get distracted

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.960
And sometimes caught up in a haze

00:02:55.960 --> 00:03:00.380
The treasure is right before my very eyes

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.040
From that initial moment onwards

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.460
I've felt the pulsing of the stars

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:10.170
When you whip your fingers across the strings

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.170
Even now it makes my heart flutter

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.040
I love you!

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:17.460
Student Council Room

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:26.790
Is something the matter?

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:27.500
Huh?

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.000
Oh, uh...

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.880
I was just thinking about
your amazing performance last week...

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:35.750
Save Them in the Music

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.380
Thank you.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:36.960
Ichigaya-san?

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.210
It's nothing!

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.830
RAS and Roselia both put
an insane amount of energy into the show...

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.210
You see, we held an evaluation...

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:45.630
"Evaluation"?

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.330
A post-performance meeting
between all of our members.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.960
Despite our best efforts,
we weren't able to compete with RAS.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:57.000
This raised a discussion regarding necessary
improvements to the quality of our live performances.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.000
Our next show is just around the corner...

00:03:59.000 --> 00:03:59.830
Next show...?

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.250
The "Over the Future" concert is this weekend.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:07.170
It's a test of sorts to judge whether or not we're ready
to participate in FUTURE WORLD FES...

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:10.750
Many who intend on appearing at
FUTURE WORLD FES play this concert.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.500
In other words, a preliminary round.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:16.130
A crucial performance measuring
the extent of our capabilities.

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:20.500
Time stops for no one, I suppose.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.790
And we intend to do everything in our power
to prepare ourselves.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.330
It's "Snappy-chan"!

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.330
Miracle Drummer

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.330
SNAPPY-CHAN

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.750
You like these books, too?!

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.170
I think the story's interesting.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:34.250
Masuki-san lent them to me.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.080
Huh?!

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.040
You home, LOCK?

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.540
I'm leavin' you some potatoes in the boiler.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.210
Sweet potatoes!

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.420
Thank you.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.670
Sure thing.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.880
Oh, didn't realize you had guests...

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:50.170
King!

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:51.670
Good afternoon.

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:53.460
Hey there.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.000
Aren't you the kid from Roselia...?

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.460
Precisely.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:01.750
Creeping forth from the gates of a Hell
governed by Roselia themselves,

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:05.790
I am a shadow, uh... creature of some sort!

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:09.040
Why are you so DAMN cute?

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.250
Actually, I was aiming for more of a "cool" vibe...

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.960
All you Roselia girls are surprisingly cute.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.710
Makin' a fuss and messin' around backstage...

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.130
I know what you mean!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.830
Even Yukina-senpai let loose
and ate a few cat-shaped cookies!

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:24.960
Really?

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:28.830
The other day, we ate a
"Super Comfort Food Combo" together!

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.080
"Super Comfort Food Combo"?

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:38.250
Losing was frustrating, but we're pumped up and
ready to focus on doing a better job next time!

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:42.040
Expect Roselia to transform into
an even COOLER version of ourselves!

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:46.420
And I'm gonna be the coolest drummer
in the history of cool drummers!

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.170
You're cooler than I thought.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:52.420
You mean it?!

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.920
I think you're cool, too!

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.380
She's right, you know!

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:58.330
Hey, I heard you like "Snappy-chan." Is it true?!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:01.460
Yeah. The ending of volume two
was badass, don'tcha think?!

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.080
That part makes me cry every time...

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.210
Catch you later!

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.290
See you tomorrow!

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:08.080
'Kay!

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:09.460
Come back and visit.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.960
Miracle Drummer

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.960
SNAPPY-CHAN

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.880
Incredible...

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:30.250
Huh?

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:32.580
LAYER-san?

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:34.040
Go ahead.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.960
No, no. It's all yours.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:37.250
Please, I insist...

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.460
Great work at the concert.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:45.920
You, too.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.250
RAS' performance was awesome!

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:52.000
Something about your bass and vocals
packed a real punch!

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:52.830
Huh?

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:55.460
Well, I...

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:05.710
You guys were...

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:14.130
I started learning to play the bass because I wanted
to form a band with Tae-chan... Tae Hanazono-chan.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:16.670
What a coincidence. I was in a similar situation.

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:18.130
Seriously?

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:20.420
Yukina's a childhood friend of mine.

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:24.670
Who would've thought we started playing bass
for the same reason?

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.330
Um...

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.130
Thank you for everything you did during the concert.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.500
Huh? What do you mean? The cookies?

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:35.080
The cookies, too...

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:39.710
Roselia's performance was eye-opening.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:44.250
Watching you... pushed me and the others
to go above and beyond.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.080
I was hesitant before...

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:50.670
But then I found myself wanting to
challenge Roselia with my skills.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:55.000
I'm truly grateful we were able to
stand on the same stage.

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:58.040
No, no, no! I'M the one who should be grateful!

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:59.210
Please, there's no need...

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:01.540
I thought you were incredible, LAYER-san.

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.250
Don't tell me... Déjà vu?

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.420
Yeah.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.580
So, were you in a band before RAS?

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:10.290
No, I wasn't.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:14.540
In fact, I'd only ever taken
temporary gigs until recently.

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:16.670
I'm headed out.

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:19.790
Good job out there, and thanks for your help!
We'll see you next time!

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:22.330
Of course. Call me anytime.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.290
Awesome!

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:35.330
Those vocals of yours have impressive potential!

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:38.920
Thanks. Are your parents around...?

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:40.580
I'm not a child!

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:42.250
Look.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:45.960
My name is CHU2, and I'm a producer.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.630
They gave me a special badge
for backstage access.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.420
A producer...?

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:54.420
Rei Wakana, I've come here to scout you.

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:56.790
You're going to join my band.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:00.040
Sorry, but I'll pass.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.170
Give me a call if you ever need a temp.

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:03.170
Goodbye.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.630
Wait!

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.540
You're my only hope!

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:15.500
Listen to this and you'll understand.
You're the only one who can sing my music!

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:19.420
You should be in the spotlight,
and my vocals will put you there!

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:25.130
I was shocked by the quality of CHU2's music.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:26.960
It almost sounded professional.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:31.540
I couldn't help but wonder how much passion and
genius she had stashed away in that tiny body.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.790
Way to go, CHU2!

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:37.750
I was happy she discovered my talent
and recognized my full potential.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:41.210
On top of that, I felt like she'd
thrown down the gauntlet...

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:42.540
What do you mean?

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:50.500
It was like a test of skill: Am I capable of expressing
such powerful music with my voice and bass?

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:54.210
Opportunities like that come along once in a lifetime.

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:56.080
Seemed worthwhile to me...

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:04.250
I'm exhausted...

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:05.960
Are you alright, Ako-chan?

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:09.170
I'm pretty tuckered out, too.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.920
My fingers are killing me!

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:13.920
Hey, you guys!

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.210
How's it going?

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:16.210
Hello!

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:17.540
You're here late.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:21.830
The big Jizo Festival waits for no one, after all!

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:23.880
Where's Sayo-san?

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:25.330
Still finishing up.

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:29.170
I think she's a little hung up over our last show...

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:31.460
She's been working even harder than usual.

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.380
You're right...

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:38.960
Well, I thought Roselia's performance
the other day was awesome!

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:40.920
Thanks!

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.960
The stickers on the board
in the lounge surprised me.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.130
The ones they used to decide who went first, right?

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:48.040
I've never seen anything like that before.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.580
Even Ran stuck hers to the Roselia side, you know.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:51.540
Huh?! Wha...?!
Even Ran stuck hers to the Roselia side, you know.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:52.380
Huh?! Wha...?!

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.460
Aww!

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:54.670
Thanks, Ran!

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:56.080
Is that true?

00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:00.290
Ta-da! Photographic evidence!

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:01.420
Knock it off, Moca!

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:02.630
They stuck 'em all over like this...

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:04.290
There's no need to be embarrassed.
They stuck 'em all over like this...

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:04.920
I am NOT embarrassed!
They stuck 'em all over like this...

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:05.540
I am NOT embarrassed!
And there's Ran's sticker.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.290
Moca

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.290
Ran

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:07.290
Himari

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:07.290
Tomoe

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:07.290
Tsugumi

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:07.290
Wasn't it amazing? Almost like a drawing or something!
And there's Ran's sticker.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:07.670
Reminded me of a yearbook or something.
And there's Ran's sticker.

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:09.500
Reminded me of a yearbook or something.
A bunch of people decided to doodle on it, too...

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.330
We believe in you, Roselia

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.330
Soar with the wings of friendship

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.330
Love you, Lisa

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:10.830
It was so sweet!
A bunch of people decided to doodle on it, too...

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:11.960
A bunch of people decided to doodle on it, too...

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.040
We're with you, Roselia

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.040
Bloom in all your glory

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.040
We're behind you in your wildest dreams

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.040
Let this day go down in history as one of triumph

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:16.710
Look, you guys! Messages to Roselia!

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:20.540
Our audience wrote them for us...

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:22.880
Wow... They made a rose!

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:25.290
Moca, can you send these to me later?

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:27.460
Roger.

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:30.500
Thanks! I'll send them to our group chat, too.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.000
Hooray!

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.210
Minato-san.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:40.130
This doesn't end here. You know that, right?

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:42.920
Of course.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:47.290
The finals are right around the corner
for RAS and Roselia.

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:49.880
I've calculated our average number of votes
in comparison to theirs.

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:51.330
Journey to the Budokan!!!

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.630
Where's this coming from all of a sudden, Arisa?

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:58.080
If our goal is the Budokan, we need to get our butts
in gear soon or else we're going to run out of time.

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.670
RAS and Roselia won't hesitate
to leave us in the dust.

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:02.830
Venue Capacity (Info via Rokka)

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:03.670
RAS always performs at Dub,

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:05.080
RAISE A SUILEN

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:05.080
Dub Capacity: 1000 x 7 Shows 6981 Votes

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:06.750
and Roselia performs about
twice as often at CiRCLE.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.670
Roselia

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.670
CiRCLE: Capacity is half of Dub's. 499 votes on average.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:08.880
We've been performing at Galaxy,

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:09.710
Poppin' Party (That's us!)

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:09.710
Galaxy's Capacity: 100 x 13 Shows 1283 Votes

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:11.750
but assuming we receive votes from
a full house, that's only 100 people.

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:11.750
Only one way to solve difference in capacity!!

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:11.750
Increase the number of performances!!!

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.380
If you do the math,

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:18.540
this means we would have to perform
ten times as often as RAS at the very LEAST.

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:19.580
TEN times?!

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:21.580
Kinda scary when you put it that way...

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:26.670
Which brings us to the current vote count:
Roselia shows no sign of slowing down.

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:29.080
The gap between us will probably continue to widen.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:33.130
At this rate, the idea of going to
the Budokan is wishful thinking.

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:35.290
Unless a giant wave swoops in
and swallows them up,

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:37.830
we aren't going to survive the preliminaries.

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:42.580
PoPiPa's ranked 30th, right?

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:45.290
Uh... 22nd!

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:46.380
Meowza...

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:47.630
We're making progress!

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:49.790
People probably saw our PoPi-V.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:50.580
Yeah!

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:51.960
Is this the wave?!

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.290
Not even close.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.290
From this point on,
we've got to get serious about the prelims.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.960
Now, let's review our schedule!

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.580
Yeah!

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.420
We should start packing up.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:11.290
Actually, I was hoping to stay
and practice for a bit longer...

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:12.330
Me, too!

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:15.250
In that case, I'll go ask the staff
if we can extend our session.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:17.790
I wouldn't mind staying a little longer, either.

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:18.920
Sound good?

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:20.380
Please do.

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:21.710
Okay!

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:25.630
Let's take a quick break.

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:29.080
I'm fired up and rarin' to go!

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.830
What about you, Rin-Rin?!

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.210
Yeah.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.080
The feast is almost upon us...

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:39.790
Crawling out of the murky abyss,
we gather to play our, um...

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.000
The forbidden, uh...

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:46.130
What's another word for "cool music"...?

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:47.540
How about "melody"?

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:50.170
A forbidden melody!

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:52.580
Their ears shall savor every moment!

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:55.540
I'm gonna go get some water!

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.920
Take your time.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.750
Yukina-san...

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:08.460
Sayo-san! Sayo-san!

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:09.290
Sayo!

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:12.790
Sayo, are you alright?! C'mon, get up!

00:14:13.130 --> 00:14:13.960
Sayo!

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:14.750
Hikawa-san!

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:16.250
Ako, go get Marina-san!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.420
R-right!

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.710
Sayo says she's going to sit out today's practice.

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:26.920
Rin-Rin told me she stayed home from school, too...

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:28.170
I see...

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:30.540
You think she's doing alright?

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:34.630
She had a fever the whole time,
and I never even noticed...

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:35.920
Me neither.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:41.210
I mean, I could tell she was working hard,
but she went way overboard.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:43.630
Let's practice individually for today.

00:14:43.630 --> 00:14:45.960
We'll schedule a full rehearsal before the concert.

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:46.960
'Kay.

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:47.960
Gotcha.

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:48.880
See you later.

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:50.630
Huh?! Hold on, Yukina!

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:51.710
Yukina-san!

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:55.000
We're coming with you!

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:58.460
Rin-Rin says she wants to
check up on Sayo-san, too!

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:00.580
How did you know...?

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.540
Don't underestimate us!

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.210
Here you go, Big Sis.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:07.710
"Ahh."

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:10.000
I'm capable of feeding myself.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:12.130
You don't want pudding?

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:14.170
I've got canned oranges, too!

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:15.960
Or should I make some porridge instead?

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:18.000
The food isn't the issue...

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:22.540
What exactly are you so happy about, anyway?

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:25.580
I'm not happy at all! This is how I show concern!

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:27.830
Hard to believe with a face like that...

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:32.380
Who could that be?

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:35.880
SAYO-SAN!

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:38.330
Udagawa-san! Relax, would you?

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.420
B-but... But you...!

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:42.960
How are you feeling?

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.330
It was only a small fever...

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:47.630
At one point, it reached 102 °!

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:51.920
I'm sorry for disrupting our schedule
right before "Over the Future"...

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.290
Your health is more important.

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:56.420
Sayo-san, is your throat scratchy?

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:58.500
We brought ice cream and fruit!

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.210
Specifically apples.

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:01.380
Mind if I borrow the kitchen?

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:03.540
Sure thing! How 'bout I go with you?

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:05.380
I'm gonna make some porridge.

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:06.580
Me, too.

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:08.000
I'll help!

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:09.880
Shall I slice the apples?

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:12.830
Don't worry. You hang out here.

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:15.170
Take a left, Rinko-chan!
How should we cut the apples?

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.040
I'm thinking bunny ears.

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:18.540
Be right back!

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:28.250
Minato-san.

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:32.830
I'm sorry for allowing this to happen
during such a crucial time.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:37.830
Looking back, I suppose I overexerted myself...

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:41.920
But I couldn't shake my feelings of regret
towards our last performance.

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:43.210
Sayo...

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:49.420
And I found myself overwhelmed with guilt because
of the messages in the pictures Imai-san sent us...

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:52.080
Messages... The stickers?

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:58.290
Those messages made me realize exactly how much
our fans were looking forward to our performance.

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:03.630
I wasn't able to live up to their expectations...

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:06.630
I knew there must be something
I could've done better...

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.580
It's so frustrating...

00:17:10.540 --> 00:17:13.420
Personally, I was happy.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:20.080
Seeing the stickers and messages made me happy.

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:22.750
It did?

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:23.960
Yes.

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:25.710
If Aoba-san hadn't...

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:30.040
If Afterglow hadn't shown us those pictures,
we would never have known.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:34.080
Besides, we gained something
as a result of that performance.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:38.580
We came face-to-face with
an audience we've yet to reach.

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:40.580
An audience we've yet to reach?

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.330
Thanks to RAISE A SUILEN.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.500
Are you referring to their promotional tactics?

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:48.670
Exactly.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:51.670
I remember discussing this at the evaluation meeting...

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:56.000
But we came to the conclusion that their approach
and objectives are different than Roselia's.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:59.080
You're right. They are different than ours.

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:03.960
Which is why we never would have had this experience
if not for our joint concert with RAISE A SUILEN.

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:08.880
Afterglow and RAISE A SUILEN...

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:12.830
There are all sorts of bands out there
made up of many different types of people.

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:15.790
In my eyes, the concert was
an opportunity for Roselia to grow

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:19.040
through an experience we otherwise
wouldn't have had on our own,

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:23.210
in order to aspire towards even greater things.

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:26.380
Minato-san...

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:33.040
So then, that's why you accepted
CHU2-san's challenge...

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:38.710
I understand.

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:45.080
We're back!

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:47.330
I cut up a bunch of apples for you!

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:49.000
There're fries, too!

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:50.710
Think you can eat some?

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:53.080
Thanks. Don't mind if I do.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:55.250
Yukina, can you hold this for a sec?

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:57.210
Sure. This looks good.

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.500
We added cheese, risotto-style.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.830
The apples are tasty too, you know!

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:04.880
I think Sayo-san fell asleep...

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:06.420
Not so loud!

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:37.750
Big Sis...?

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:41.420
Aren't you forgetting to knock?

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:47.210
Your fever's going to spike again
if you don't get some rest.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:50.040
I know.

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:51.540
But...

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:54.750
I want to save these feelings in the music...

00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:06.080
Please wait until we've officially opened the doors!

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:09.080
Same-day tickets are sold out!

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:15.330
Is it just me, or did that feel amazing?!

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:16.210
Yeah!

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:17.000
Agreed.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:21.080
Thank you for making extra rehearsal time
right before the concert.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:24.210
I'd planned on it from the beginning,
even if you hadn't asked.

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:26.380
Are you feeling better?

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:28.790
Yes. Way better.

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:31.580
I should be in perfect condition
to perform at the concert.

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:36.000
The version of us today is different from
the people we were yesterday.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.210
Very true.

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:40.000
I'm worn out and pumped up at the same time!

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:41.580
M-me, too!

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:43.960
Now... Let's do this!

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:50.710
Big Sis!

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:54.080
It's time... Roselia's up next.

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:55.920
You think they'll be alright?

00:20:57.920 --> 00:20:59.880
Allow me to introduce our members.

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:02.670
On guitar: Sayo Hikawa!

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:08.420
On bass: Lisa Imai!

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:11.040
Are you guys having fun?

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:13.500
On drums: Ako Udagawa!

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:16.130
Gold medal!

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:18.830
On keyboard: Rinko Shirokane!

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:23.630
And our lead vocalist: Yukina Minato!

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:29.500
Everyone...

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:39.000
I'd like to thank you for
your never-ending love and support.

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:53.000
Now, let's burn brightly once more!

00:21:56.380 --> 00:21:58.040
Burning up!

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:01.250
Burning up!

